{"name":"Demeter","hex":"#ecda9e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Demeter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The goddess of the fertility of the Earth and harvests, protector of marriage and social order; daughter of Cronos and Rhea, mother to Persephone.","1108 Demeter, a main belt asteroid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Demeter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Demeter","blocks":[{"text":"In ancient Greek religion and mythology, Demeter is the Olympian goddess of the harvest and agriculture, presiding over crops, grains, food, and the fertility of the earth. Although Demeter is mostly known as a grain goddess, she also appeared as a goddess of health, birth, and marriage, and had connections to the Underworld. She is also called Deo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Demeter_Altemps_Inv8546.jpg/330px-Demeter_Altemps_Inv8546.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demeter"},{"title":"Demeter (cat)","blocks":[{"text":"Demeter is a main character in the Andrew Lloyd Webber musical Cats. The musical is an adaptation of T. S. Eliot's 1939 poetry book Old Possum's Book of Practical Cats, and the character's name is given in the poem \"The Naming of Cats\". Demeter is a very troubled and skittish female Jellicle cat. The role was originated by Sharon Lee-Hill in the West End in 1981, and by Wendy Edmead on Broadway in 1982. Daniela Norman played this role in the 2019 film adaptation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9b/Demeter_1998_Cats_film.png/330px-Demeter_1998_Cats_film.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demeter_(cat)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Didrachme_de_l%27%C3%AEle_de_Paros.jpg/500px-Didrachme_de_l%27%C3%AEle_de_Paros.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut